{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527707-antediluvian-hide-and-seek","id":1527707,"title":"Antediluvian hide and seek","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-01T14:26:52-08:00","id":1527707,"title":"Antediluvian hide and seek","content":"When you read the lore antediluvian are godly powerfull, ravnos survived atomic bomb with fortitude, Domination could be used on whole humanity, same for vicissitude, and the more i read about how powerfull are level 10 discipline the more i wonder why the hell did they disappeared?<br /> <br /> I couldn't find something yet, but i assume it has to be something serious. Is the answer in old edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T04:46:06-08:00","id":1527766,"title":"","content":"<b>Veddhartha</b> - The Venture Antediluvian, some sources says was destroyed by the Brujah Antediluvian/team of Brujah in the either first or either second city, yet he embraces left and right, till 60 BC when he embraced Antonius and Erik Eigermann/Ueruic and Danava believe themselves to be the guardians of their Antediluvian (pitri, or &quot;father&quot;), whom they call Veddhartha. These Danava claim that the Ventrue are in fact an errant antitribu bloodline of the Danava.<br /> So the best is at the moment, he is sleeping and the Danava are gurding his torpid body<br /> <br /> <b>Ilyes</b> - the Brujah Antediluvan diableire by Troile is not that certain; not even the date or explained the fact why the others not punished her (after all, the first diablerie of an Antediluvan - back than just an elder - would set up a dangerous precedent if not punished)<br /> So Troile is either Ilyes, whos mind shattered by the experience and emotions or as per Gehenna sourcbook, Ilyes hurled himself to the Future at the moment of his Diablerie and landed in Lilith's Garden<br /> <br /> <b>Troile</b> - IF she is not Ilyes, then she in torpor trapped under Carthage ruins hugging Moloch, sealed by a powerful ritual devised by Cybelle<br /> <br /> <b>Laza Omri Baras</b> - the Lasombra Antediluvian died, bot got better. in theory he was eaten by a flock of rebels, lead by Grationo... yet nobody can recall the exact event, and Grationo never claimed the &quot;throne&quot; (they were totally dominated) nor became a 3rd generation vampire. All and all, the Lasombra Antediluvian became an Abyssal Entity when he entered the Qlippoth of Primodial Darkness<br /> <br /> <b>Sutekh</b> - Vanished 33 AD. Lurking in Duat... but the Ventrue Nasch, the Circassian came upon a cult known as the Coil of the Lion that allegedly harbored the torpid body of the Antediluvian in the 14th century. When Nasch opened the sarcophagus that held the body, the last thing he heard was the sound of a thousand serpents rending the air with their unearthly hissing as the chamber around him vanished into blackness. He found himself standing upon a dais in a vast, open temple situated on an otherwise empty expanse of desert that stretched into infinity. Before him lay the body of a man with the head of an unspeakable beast, no sarcophagus in sight, naked but for a simple loincloth. Nasch managed to drink from the torpid creature, but the experience overwhelmed him and sent him to Torpor for more than a decade<br /> Actually the two version is not mutually exclusive, it is possible he is in Duat an the Coil of the Lion is guarding a portal<br /> <br /> <b>Saulot </b>- Tremere ate him. Then he got better. The P'o of Saulot became the White Worm of Vienna, the Hun visited Hunedoara Castle and the Inconnu, then wandered away<br /> <br /> <b>Sargon </b>- The Cappadocian Antediluvan bacame a Wraith after Augustus tried to eat him, then In Giovanni Chronicles IV: Nuova Malattia, the Children of Isaac tried to put him to rest with a ritual from Marianna. Partially worked. During Gehenna, his soul was consumed when the Sixth Great Maelstrom hit the Shadowlands and became a Specter, a de-facto part of Oblivion.<br /> <br /> <b>Malkav</b>\u200b - After the fall of the Second City, Malkav is believed to have traveled towards the city of Petra. It is along this journey that some think the Eldest Malkavian was attacked and torn asunder. Malkav has likely become the Madness Network, a psychic link connecting virtually all members of Clan Malkavian. However, other accounts state that the Malkavian Antediluvian continues to sleep under Petra, or that he rests beneath Jerusalem... but it turned out, it is his twin sister, <b>Malakai</b><br /> <br /> <b>Malakai </b>- Some scriptures (Beckett's Jyhad Diary, Gehenna and in \u200bThe Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra) claim he had a twin sister, Malakai, Black Hand scriptures say Malakai is imprisoned deep within the Shadowlands because she is so mad and powerful that she warps reality around her. (Malakai is mentioned in the Shaal Fragment as an antediluvian who seeks &quot;peace&quot; during the first Gehenna. However, since Arikel is said to seek unity, the peace Malakai seeks may not be diplomatic in nature. Rather, she could have sought peace by journeying to the Shadowlands or entering Torpor.)<br /> Beckett's Jyhad Diary suggest, she sleeps under Jerusalem<br /> <br /> <b>Nahema </b>- Chaining the Beast mentions one branch of the Path of Lilith, the Path of Awakening. The followers of it believes that Arikel and Malkav were twins, children of Lilith, and that they had a younger sister, Nahema, who also received the Embrace. According to legend, Nahema descended into Hell, but never lost touch with her siblings, her spirit forever bound to them and their childer \u2013 it is Nahema's spirit that whispers in the Malkavian Madness Network, that burns in the hearts of the Toreador. Some of her worshippers call her the Dark Muse, the Anti-Muse, and the Demon Queen of Madness, and she is said to be patron saint of serial killers and torturers<br /> <br /> <b>The Eldest </b>- masquerading as Lugoj, let his body be transported to a hidden crypt beneath what would become New York City by Zantosa Revenants that knew of his ruse. There, it entered a meditative state to reach Metamorphosis. In the process, its body dissolved to a puddle of slime, then transformed into fungi, then into plants and every other living creature in existence, exploring the infinitude of life by assuming its shape. It started to infuse itself into other creatures, beginning with plants and animals, to master them and unite all Creation into itself. The Eldest appears to have had more trouble than it should in its quest, lost in itself looking for an answer it could not find, riven by the loss of its true bonds to the Earth. Eventually, sometime in the early 21st century, it found its way back to itself, then left New York to seek its siblings' counsel<br /> <br /> <b>Haqim </b>- The last time anyone has seen the Banu Haqim Antediluvian was in the British Isles in 121 CE, where he was engaged in philosophical conversations with the Ventrue Prince of London, Mithras - which is interesting by itself, since Mithras would be diablerized in 1996 by one of Haqim's own descendants...\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <b>Absimiliard</b>. - The time the Nosferatu Antediluvian fell in torpor, he was fighting Baba Yaga in Russia milleniums ago. Has spent a long time in torpor at Enoch, but he probably awoke recently in Eastern European mountains. [Cb-To] has him and Arikel meeting in 2nd century Rome. He has planned a nuclear attack in 2000, but with a little help of Kupala, that was avoided. According Gehenna, he retreated back under the Atlentic Ocean to breed Kaiju-like monsters<br /> <br /> <b>Arikel </b>and <b>Ishtar - </b>the Toreador Antediluvians are interesting.<br /> As for Arikel, the Toreador scholars claim that their clan's Antediluvian was killed in the time of Enoch by the plotting of Absimiliard and Set, progenitors of the Nosferatu and Setite clans, who supposedly cut out and ate her heart. Yet, there are records that indicate that she had not experienced Final Death, and had awakened from Torpor around 260 BCE, acting as an advisor to Prince Alchias.<br /> Ishtar tried to take the Tablet of Destiny from either Ennoia or either Enkidu Outraged by this action, Ennoia set out to kill the Toreador Antediluvian and tracked Ishtar to Sumer. Ishtar fled but not before unleashing upon them some great monster known as the Bull of Heaven, while she escaped to Crete. In Crete, Ishtar resided with King Minos, who desired and demanded her gift. Initially, she refused, but then compromised to embrace his son. Unworthy of the embrace, the son fell into the clutches of the Beast. His erratic behavior had him imprisoned by his father Minos, in what was an underground maze.<br /> Both of the Toreador Antediluvians went off the map, but were in Greece<br /> Worth to mention, there is a Toreador bloodline/Laibon Legacy called the Ishatrri claim to be descended from the Babylonian goddess Ishtar, they are the only Laibon Legacy that are not native to Africa; however, through manipulation and diplomacy, they have become an important part of Laibon culture.<br /> <br /> <b>Ennoia -</b> It is suggested that Ennoia fell into a long torpor around the time of Christ and there is debate as to whether she has woken up from it yet.<br /> <br /> <b>Zapatashura</b> - Hisdeath was described in deatail, and considered dead, yet even in V5 there are hints (blood of Zapatashura) maybe he is not THAT dead<br /> Like how Malkav was tore apart, yet his children consumed his blood to shiled it from the sun, so he survived as the Cobweb/Madnes network... if that trick worked with Malkav, Zapatashura may survived too, since the sun not destroyed his lifeblood.... or it was just a reality alteration<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere </b>- after Saulot evicted him from his owm body (either in the dark ages, right after he tried to diablerize him - witch mean Saulot did a very dirty on his own clan - or in 1998) his spirit fled and is now in Goratrix body.\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <b>Augustus</b> - lies in torpor in the Mausoleum, Venice. Then after V5, in pieces\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 01-03-2024, 01:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T08:46:42-08:00","id":1527773,"title":"","content":"The precise answer(s) to the question of why the Antediluvians, collectively, chose to disappear is one of those things you kind of need to settle for yourself to some extent. But the short answer is &quot;the Jyhad.&quot;<br /> <br /> Accepting the traditional Noddist narrative, the Antediluvians are all too aware that, despite their incredible powers, they are not invincible. Otherwise they likely would not have been able to overthrow the Second Generation. You also have at least two of the truly ancient Antediluvians, [Ventrue] and [Brujah], who have at least possibly been sent to their Final Deaths, in some fashion or another by their peers.<br /> <br /> That doesn't include the cases we know of where the Antediluvians were thwarted by non-vampires. You've already mentioned what the Technocracy did to [Ravnos], and its worth mentioning that magic of the modern era is frequently regarded as having weaknesses or limits that did not exist in the past. [Set] was similarly defeated in his home territory by the various allies of the Osirian League, even though it came with a heavy price.<br /> <br /> All of this is to say that there are dangers in the world that even the Antediluvians cannot just dismiss (depending on the version of the story you go with), so like other vampires they hide themselves in the shadows as a survival tactic, just a lot deeper and more effectively due to their age and power.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that torpor is just something old vampires find it harder and harder to resist. And the Antediluvians are OLD. So if you're going to be forced into a turbo-nap, it's probably a good idea to make sure no one can bother you in the mean time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T11:02:18-08:00","id":1527777,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> As powerful as they are, it's been proven that they are not unstoppable as we seen them do in the 2nd generation childer of Caine and most are aware that they other powers out there that can rival them in power and duplicity and keeping a low profile is the wisest course for them to pursue there plans in some measure of peace.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T12:06:25-08:00","id":1527780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527707-antediluvian-hide-and-seek?p=1527777#post1527777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As powerful as they are, it's been proven that they are not unstoppable as we seen them do in the 2nd generation childer of Caine<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you mention...<br /> Techically, not many 2nd Generation children of Caine died <i>by</i> the hand of the Antediluvians if we consider the various clan lores<br /> <br /> <b>The Lovers</b> (Clanbook: Toreador Revised, p. 15)<br /> The pair had hoped one night to combine their flesh as in the spirit, making a new soul that held the best of each of them - instead they were doomed to suffer in eternity as two beings, never joined in soul through offspring. Rather than accept that fate, they walked into the sun.<br /> Caine was so overcome with grief that he forbade their names to ever be spoken.<br /> They are dead, but by their own hand<br /> <br /> <b>Khe-duk</b> and <b>Liada</b>, aka. the King and Queen of En'esh (Clan Book: Assamite)<br /> They were killed by Haqim who Embraced himself with their blood<br /> So they are dead<br /> <br /> <b>Enoch/Ynosh/En'esh, the Prince, son of Khe-duk and Liada </b>(Clan Book: Assamite, Book of Nod, various other)<br /> Beckett's Jyhad Diary, p. 529-540 offers the possibility, He was in the Sarcophagus Beckett and co unearthed<br /> So he potentially survived<br /> <br /> <b>Zillah, the Beautiful </b>(Caine's Chosen: The Black Hand, Children of the Revolution)<br /> She became the Weeping Stone, a sacred relic and pilgrimage site for the Lost Tribe (the modern Black Hand) in the mountainous region of modern Iraq. The stone itself is tall, lushly curved, and planted deep in the earth. The coppery smell of blood wafts from it on the wind as one gets closer.<br /> When Zillah saw that her brother was dead and she was next, she wept and cried out to Father Caine. He heard her pleas and took pity on her, changing her into a stone so that she would not be found and killed. But still she continued to mourn, and her blood-tears continued to flow from the Stone, just as they do to this very night. To taste the Stone is to taste the last remaining Blood of the faithful generation.<br /> <br /> <b>Irad, the Strong</b><br /> Cults of the Blood Gods revealed Servitors of Irad. According to Noddist history, Irad was the most bloodthirsty warmonger of his time, his prowess on the battlefield and in commanding men earning the respect of the first murderer, and Caine\u2019s Embrace. Irad joined the ranks of the Second Generation and led Caine\u2019s armies for an unrecorded number of centuries, always loyal to his sire and kin, as long as the battlefield could slake his unquenchable thirst.<br /> Something changed in Irad when the Antediluvians rebelled against the Second Generation, however, with the handful of accounts from vampires who claim to remember the war agreeing Irad turned his armies to oppose Enoch, Zillah, and a controversially vague number of other Second Generation vampires.<br /> His motives for doing so are unclear to this night, though some posit he felt the Third Generation could bring him the blood he so craved in greater quantities than his sire and siblings. While others believe Caine snubbed him as nothing more than a killer, goading Irad into showing him what a killer he could be.<br /> On the other hand, In The Legend of Irad, at some point in the First City, Irad &quot;The Strong&quot; sought to purge himself of all evil. Using his mastery of Protean, the Ancient gathered all of his evil into a bilious mass of repugnancy and horror, and spat it out, fed it to a Mage. Enoch later Embraced It zhus, the world was given the Tzimisce Antediluvian<br /> Maybe Irad lost it that made him so fierce and bloodthirsty....<br /> He was slain eventually, to his outmost surprise, so... dead<br /> <br /> <b>The First Born (Clan Book: Toreador p.12)</b><br /> Caine left the First City and encountered a tribe of nomad in the desert. Among the nomads was a youth of great beuty. Caine took the youth back to the First City, watched the child to grow and when the child became an adult, made his beloved First Born.<br /> &quot;A Frightening Legacy&quot; Legend has it, however, that the First Born, sire of Arikel survived. Escaping in to the desert the First Born followed the setting sun as his father had done and was never heard from again.<br /> <br /> <b>Ravnos </b>(Clan Book: Ravnos p.13)<br /> &quot;Caine's Favord Son&quot;<br /> He died when he was nailed to the rooftop of the great temple to greet the sunrise (city is unnamed, but was a vampire city and in beauty and majesty it rivaled Enoch, but in the streets hung the stale aura of death)<br /> <br /> <b>The Crone </b>(Book of Nod)<br /> In order to win the heart of Zillah, Caine sought out the Crone, who taught him how to blood bond Zillah to himself. In exchange, the Crone enslaved Caine through her own blood bond and forced Caine to Embrace her. She also took a number of Caine's descendants to herself; these Cainites were never seen again. Presumably, she devoured them. A year and a day after the Crone first enslaved Caine, the blood bond faded, and Caine staked her and left her to burn in the sun.<br /> But not checked the kill...<br /> The Lhiannan bloodline claim to be descendants of the Crone.<br /> According to their own lore, the first Lhiannan was created when the Crone infused a woodland spirit into a vampire. This spirit was said to be a desperate, jealous being that could apparently see that people would destroy the forests and burn the trees that comprised them. Joining with an undying predator, then, was apparently the spirit's attempt at dodging this fate. Whether or not any of that is true, the Lhiannan did have a connection to the natural world that no other vampire, not even the Gangrel, could equal.<br /> <br /> <b>Namrael, the Enochian </b>(The Midnight Circus)<br /> Described as a daughter of Caine who left &quot;the undead city of her sire&quot; in the time of the First City to join what became the Midnight Circus<br /> She sacrificed herself in a rite, bleed to death to feed her power, to strengthen the Incarna &quot;Cara&quot; an ancient spirit of the Cult that later become the Circus, so it could continue to exist<br /> <br /> <b>Azaneal </b>(Clanbook: Baali, The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra)<br /> He is seemingly a powerful Baali methuselah, leader of a new Baali branch and believed to be the founder of the Angellis Ater.<br /> However.... Elioud scholars of the Tal'Mahe'Ra cite Azaneal as the name of a Second Generation vampire who had been partially diablerized by one or more Antediluvians, but he had managed to retreat as a manner of disembodied demonic spectre to a Qlippoth realm; if true the current being called Azaneal then would be the husk of a Baali methuselah of unknown name possessed by the demonic spectre of a Second Generation vampire.<br /> <br /> <b>Aretstikapha</b><br /> The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra cites ten Second Generation vampires, seven of whom had departed to Lilith's garden realm D\u2019hainu; two who went to D'hainu are named: Aretstikapha and Azaneal.<br /> <br /> The Erciyes Fragments list the following vampires, of what it says, are Second Generation:<br /> Enoch<br /> Zyllah<br /> Jabal<br /> Adah<br /> Tubal<br /> Mehujael<br /> Out of these Enoch and Zilah/Zyllah is somewhat easy, the other four is a mistery, except one:<br /> <b>Jabal, the Master of Servants</b>, (The Book of Nod, The Erciyes Fragments) was the first Ghoul. He was created by Caine during the time of the First City.<br /> One of the childer of Caine mentioned in the Erciyes Fragments is also named Jabal. It is unclear if this Jabal and the Master of Servants were the same being.<br /> His fate following the Deluge remains unrecorded, but some claim that the first ghoul is still alive underneath a secret temple in Egypt, guarding a significant quantity of Caine's blood.<br /> <br /> <b>Dracian </b>(Clanbook: Ravnos Revised, World of Darkness: Gypsies)<br /> Dracian was the name of a thief that was Embraced by Irad in order to spy on the third generation. Irad suspected the other third generation neonates of plotting against the three members of the second generation and their sire. Dracian, for his part, took to the plot like a fish to water. He was at heart a selfish man, and becoming one of the typically selfish Cainite only deepened that trait.<br /> Buuuuut<br /> According to Roma lore, Dracian has been appointed as the creator of a tree that was the embodiment life and knowledge, full in its age and beauty. It is said that one of the golden fruits of this Tree of Knowledge could cure the eternal thirst for blood in a vampire (as well as bestowing other unknown gifts). Some sources claim Dracian to be a member of the second Generation, Embraced by Caine himself during his wanderings and the sire of the Ravnos Antediluvian and Ennoia, who betrayed him and was cast out of the First City as a result.<br /> He is a maybe 2nd generation, and wandered to the East, like many others... Amriat destroyed him<br /> <br /> <b>Amriat</b><i> (</i>World of Darkness: Gypsies)<br /> He is a maybe 2nd generation, and destroyed Dracian in his desire to take the Tree of Knowledge and its fruit for himself.<br /> Like Dracian could be a 3rd Generation vampire. It is a bit murky.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 01-03-2024, 05:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T12:37:43-08:00","id":1527781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527707-antediluvian-hide-and-seek#post1527707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the more i wonder why the hell did they disappeared?</div> </div> </div> </div>The true nature of the antedeluvians and the eschatology of Gehenna has never been defined so you have to come up with your own reasons. But there are lots of things (some contradictory) scattered throughout the books that you can pick and choose.<br /> <br /> One thing to remember is that the antedeluvians don't necessarily &quot;hide&quot; because they want to. Very old vampires &quot;naturally&quot; want to go into torpor and seem to metamorphosize into a different instar of their evolution. Methusalehs eventually become incapable of drinking animal or human blood and then can only feed on vampire vitae. That may not be the extent of the change.<br /> <br /> It's entirely possible that it is a natural process for vampires to eventually go into torpor and change. We just don't know what that kind of change is or how long it takes to accomplish because there simply there hasn't been enough time yet. Maybe it is limited to the antedeluvians because they hail from the antedeluvian world which had different rules than the postdeluvian world. It's entirely possible Gehenna is just the future time period when such changes are completed, and any surviving antedeluvians will naturally awake to end this current world and begin the process of the next one that will replace it.<br /> <br /> One Gehenna cult believes that the reduction of magic in this world puts more and more metaphysical burden on the godlike antedeluvians, and as long as the level of magic remains low the antedeluvians will continue to slumber. But should the level of magic increase, the antedeluvians will awaken and regain their full powers. In this explanation, it is not a function of vampire nature that explains antedeluvians slumbering, but a consequence of the status of the world around them. Even if this specific theory is not true, there could be other environmental reasons for why they slumber or awake. Maybe some kind of supernatural cycle.<br /> <br /> Then there is the belief that the antedeluvians are choosing to hide in purpose - to avoid each other in the Jyhad, to avoid other incredibly powerful beings likewise considered to be players in the Jyhad (like the mummy Horus), or perhaps from other beings (like the Secret Masters of Ventrue lore). Revealing yourself too soon just makes you a target. Or perhaps they are active - but just on a different plane of existence that is unknowable to beings in the physical world of mortals, and they'll only return to their physical bodies for specific reasons.<br /> <br /> There could be other factors or a combination of factors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 01-14-2024, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T13:09:37-08:00","id":1527782,"title":"","content":"So, in short, some have been killed, other defeated and put to slumber, and the rest are waiting in torpor. The main interrogation is in the fact that the level 10 Discipline is plot and allow them to do whatever they like in possibly planetary proportion, if they were so powerful it is hard (for me) to understand how they could have been defeated, especially for those who've been diablerised. <br /> <br /> There's a huge gap between level 9 of let's say vicissitude that let you fuse with the land around, communicate with the passer-by and the level 10 that allow to trigger a mutation in every living being in the world (from what i've read). <br /> <br /> I'm not saying it's impossible to beat them, in other plot werewolves could be able to kill maejlin with huge risk and effort and that would not rely on a single power or physical stats, so a ritual to weaken them, a (very) smart plan or anything could work even for humans vampires hunters. It's just that if we imagine Aupex let it's user detect any kind of threats and know who, when and how he will be attack it make thing nearly impossible, same for Domination that would allow it's user to just force everyone to obey and never try to kill or even harm him...<br /> <br /> Give a plot level of power to the vampire discipline seems to be like giving them a sphere of true magic at maximum strength with less success needed to accomplish godly feats","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T14:18:21-08:00","id":1527785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527707-antediluvian-hide-and-seek?p=1527782#post1527782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Give a plot level of power to the vampire discipline seems to be like giving them a sphere of true magic at maximum strength with less success needed to accomplish godly feats</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't (necessarily) automatically give them easier access to God-like feats, but that is pretty much how I conceive of Level 10 Disciplines: complete mastery on a level that lets you employ the core concept/power of the Discipline in any way you can imagine.<br /> <br /> You are definitely right that the Antediluvians are packing some serious heat. But pretty much every gameline has some kind of entities on a level where they wield their own Plot Device level powers. If an Ante starts throwing around their weight too much, imagine what might happen if Helios had an opinion on the matter.<br /> <br /> Finally, I think it's important to remember that &quot;Plot Device&quot;-as-Discipline is not meant as a concrete power that has been balanced against other abilities. It's simply making it explicit that the Antediluvians are as powerful as they need to be for the purpose of *your* story. The examples from Gehenna are pretty intense, but you're not obligated to have your Antediluvians be that strong.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T17:07:16-08:00","id":1527791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527707-antediluvian-hide-and-seek?p=1527785#post1527785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Finally, I think it's important to remember that &quot;Plot Device&quot;-as-Discipline is not meant as a concrete power that has been balanced against other abilities. It's simply making it explicit that the Antediluvians are as powerful as they need to be for the purpose of *your* story. The examples from Gehenna are pretty intense, but you're not obligated to have your Antediluvians be that strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personnaly for my story purpose i took the Plot device as &quot;the st create his own ultimate discipline power&quot;. That way i can set something that fits my narrative needs while reducing the huge power gap between level 9 and 10.<br /> <br /> Anyway how much do you use the actual lore for your story for the case of the antediluvians? Do you prefer stick to everything you can get in the differents books/editions or do you keep the basic lore of core books and take only what you need in the lore (or nothing at all for complete narrative freedom)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T18:37:31-08:00","id":1527794,"title":"","content":"One thing to consider is that it doesn't have to be the case that antedeluvians achieved any rank 10 or even 9 in a Discipline during the time they were active. Maybe they didn't have any. Maybe they only achieved it after thousands of years in torpor. Maybe they'll only achieve once they awake from torpor when Gehenna begins. The power levels of the antedeluvians that they have in the 21st century is not what they had during 15th century or in 4000 BC or 6000 BC. I imagine they were probably still powerful when they first awoke after the Flood, but maybe that was only at the level of powerful elder.<br /> <br /> The idea that the antdeluvians can be do whatever they want is mainly an artifact of the game developers not wanting to hear stupid stuff about players telling them at cons that they defeated an antedeluvian and gained their powers, in the same way Gary Gygax didn't want to hear about players telling him how they killed Thor or Zeus after Deities &amp; Demigods was published. At any point and period in time, the antedeluvians only need to have as much power as you require them to serve the narrative need. If you think having certain powers at certain periods of time doesn't make sense given the lore and history, it's probably a good sign they didn't have them yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T19:50:16-08:00","id":1527806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527707-antediluvian-hide-and-seek?p=1527791#post1527791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personnaly for my story purpose i took the Plot device as &quot;the st create his own ultimate discipline power&quot;. That way i can set something that fits my narrative needs while reducing the huge power gap between level 9 and 10.<br /> <br /> Anyway how much do you use the actual lore for your story for the case of the antediluvians? Do you prefer stick to everything you can get in the differents books/editions or do you keep the basic lore of core books and take only what you need in the lore (or nothing at all for complete narrative freedom)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I also (jokingly) have Caine be the only one with Disciplines at 11. Half reflecting the lore that he has the unique power over the Disciplines themselves, and just as a cheap &quot;up to 11&quot; lark.<br /> <br /> I do sympathize with your situation. I also prefer the Antediluvians as &quot;Vampires, but bigger and badder&quot; rather than genuine gods with some special metaphysical function in reality. As I kind of mentioned, while I like treating level 10 Disciplines as limited only by the imagination and the power/concept of the Discipline itself, I am far less inclined to give them any special advantages in terms of the scale of their power. One of the hypothetical limiters on the Antediluvians getting out of control is Vitae. The rulebooks themselves never define the Blood Pool or spending limits of the Third Generation, but if you give their Plot Hole powers a noteworthy cost in Vitae, and put reasonable constraints on the Blood Pool available to them, then it helps to balance things out a fair bit. Even if they can do some downright insane shit if they're willing to go all-in, it may not be sustainable if they find themselves in a drawn-out conflict or facing multiple opponents with a comparable power level. Which incentivizes even these god-like monsters to walk *softly* as they carry their big sticks around.<br /> <br /> I mostly embrace the post-modern chaos of World of Darkness lore. I'd probably say that I'm happy to draw on content regardless of edition for IC lore, legends, etc. Regarding what's actually true from a Storyteller/OOC perspective, I generally try to stick as close to &quot;canon&quot; as possible, but there are inevitable contradictions, and I let my own agenda and preferences determine how I resolve the conflict. There are times where I wish for a more &quot;solid&quot; answer, especially when you get the grey areas that result from multiple ambiguities intersecting, and a lot of the issues that I haven't actually settled for myself come from stuff like that.<br /> <br /> Just one fun idea to share that I think was inspired by BJD is the idea that the diminishing power of Generation and (probably) the Clan Curses are something caused by the Antediluvians, not Caine. In particular, the idea that the rebellious assholes who rose up and murdered their sires would reasonably fear the same fate, and did *something* to ensure that the power of their descendants would diminish to prevent that danger.<br /> <br /> I'm also quite willing to take inspiration from other folks online. My preferred approach to the mess that is Saulot is somewhere between &quot;strongly inspired&quot; and &quot;blatantly taken&quot; from an idea that I got trawling around on the forums or Reddit; I didn't think to save the source at the time, and my minds wandered so much since then that I can't recall all the details. But then, even I'm still struggling on how I want to handle some of those details...<br /> <br /> It helps that there's almost nothing *really* locked into &quot;canon&quot; when it comes to the Antediluvians. Even <u>Gehenna</u> takes a pretty firm stand that you can take or leave whatever they have to say about the Antediluvians in that book, even the little blurbs at the beginning that they acknowledge as their &quot;&quot;canon&quot;&quot; answers regarding the fates of the Antes. If you like the idea of the Antediluvians as this menacing terror in the background, then you're welcome to have them be real. And if you're not really a fan, you can have them be far weaker than they are believed to be, or even already dead and gone.<br /> <br /> Finally, it's worth noting that my experience in actual play is barely existent. I've been chewing on answering the various mysteries of the World of Darkness in my personal canon for years now, but I mostly haven't had the opportunity to explore those ideas in depth with players. So there are limits to the value of my opinion lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T00:48:40-08:00","id":1527820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527707-antediluvian-hide-and-seek?p=1527806#post1527806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just one fun idea to share that I think was inspired by BJD is the idea that the diminishing power of Generation and (probably) the Clan Curses are something caused by the Antediluvians, not Caine. In particular, the idea that the rebellious assholes who rose up and murdered their sires would reasonably fear the same fate, and did *something* to ensure that the power of their descendants would diminish to prevent that danger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually i had the same reflection, the idea of the blood becoming weaker generation after generation for immortal being has always seems weird to me unless it is a curse the allow the still existing Antediluvians to come back at a time where there's no vampire powerfull enough to be a real threats for them. That idea would also fit with the concept of an exagerated interpretation of their actual power.<br /> I had even imagined a lore special condition to allows some vampire to free themselves from this curse when the gehenna come by mixing rules with the requiem (with blood potency as the original condition of their evolution) and a plot artefact/ritual they must discover/create.<br /> Never used and develop that idea further yet, but maybe in future story's","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T01:02:05-08:00","id":1527822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527707-antediluvian-hide-and-seek?p=1527820#post1527820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unless it is a curse</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, it is Caine's doing<br /> It's in Erciyes Fragments, page 91:<br /> <b>Let our proud blood weaken with each generation,<br /> So that no childe can match its sire's strength<br /> Or rise up against those who came before.<br /> So shall you be bound to peace,<br /> Enslaved by weakness where force has failed.</b><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 01-03-2024, 04:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T03:29:36-08:00","id":1527827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527707-antediluvian-hide-and-seek?p=1527822#post1527822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is, it is Caine's doing<br /> It's in Erciyes Fragments, page 91:<br /> <b>Let our proud blood weaken with each generation,<br /> So that no childe can match its sire's strength<br /> Or rise up against those who came before.<br /> So shall you be bound to peace,<br /> Enslaved by weakness where force has failed.</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh i suspected it and i was right without knowing, so theoretically every vampire should be as powerfull as Cain or be able to evolve with age with blood potency of the requiem book, fascinating! It would also meen that it could be canceled with (godly) powerful way<br /> It give Cain even more wisdom that i was aware of","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T06:36:27-08:00","id":1527838,"title":"","content":"By the way is Cain supposed to show himself during the Gehenna? I remember something about him creating and ruling new enoch city after killing vampires...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T10:00:59-08:00","id":1527851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527707-antediluvian-hide-and-seek?p=1527838#post1527838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way is Cain supposed to show himself during the Gehenna? I remember something about him creating and ruling new enoch city after killing vampires...</div> </div> </div> </div>He did show up in the Gehenna novel hanging out with Beckett, though the Gangrel didn't know it was Caine until the end of the story. But the hints were there as he kept displaying no fear about his welfare if I recall correctly and sent a band of Banu Haqim fleeing by looking at them closely when he was alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T10:17:31-08:00","id":1527852,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> Anyway how much do you use the actual lore for your story for the case of the antediluvians? Do you prefer stick to everything you can get in the differents books/editions or do you keep the basic lore of core books and take only what you need in the lore (or nothing at all for complete narrative freedom)?[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> In our game we try to keep to the basic lore of the game, but we do take some liberties with the setting with the following.<br /> <br /> The 3rd generation have largely ignored the activities of their clans and will only act if they so annoying and swat them like the comparative insects they are and in general don't bother with the nightly affairs of undead society and let there direct childer, grandchiler, or great grandchilder handle that stuff.<br /> <br /> Of the 3rd generation that might take an interest at all is Malkav as he uses the network to figure out what he saw in ancient times that upended his beliefs and having different eyes might help him solve this puzzle and that he more sane and rational then his &quot;siblings&quot; know. Set is another whom might be guiding his clan towards his goals of reshaping the world to his liking. The rest are basically missing in action<br /> <br /> The 4th to 6th generation kindred still direct things, but they are reclusive and feeling the need to sleep or feel the Beckoning stir them for reasons they don't understand and now the real movers and shakers of Kindred society are members of the 7th to 11th generations. <br /> <br /> The Sabbat has crumbled as they discovered that they didn't kill the Eldest or Lasombra at all and found there will to fight break, but there is still some bands roaming around.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T10:42:47-08:00","id":1527856,"title":"","content":"Never run a campaign with one directly involved as the &quot;mastermind in the shadow&quot;, a mysterious victim or insoluble event that could be attributed by an eventual Antediluvian? With the Gehenna approaching, it might be interesting to include signs of their return in the story, to create anxiety in pc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T11:11:08-08:00","id":1527860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527707-antediluvian-hide-and-seek?p=1527827#post1527827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh i suspected it and i was right without knowing, so theoretically every vampire should be as powerfull as Cain or be able to evolve with age with blood potency of the requiem book, fascinating! It would also meen that it could be canceled with (godly) powerful way<br /> It give Cain even more wisdom that i was aware of</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, attributing &quot;wisdom&quot; to Caine is a bit of an iffy proposition. But yes, the most common conception is that the limits of Generation were Caine trying to prevent something like the murders of the Second Generation from happening again. I've tended more towards an indifferent or uninvolved Caine in my versions of events, which is why the Antediluvians being behind the diminishing power of newer vampires made sense to me. The only flaw is that it mostly only makes sense if you view all of the Antediluvians as self-serving assholes, which gets complicated if you want to leave room for genuinely good(ish) ones who wouldn't kneecap their own descendants out of fear. Also, you start having to try and figure out Blood Potency as a connected but largely distinct system; from what little I know about V5, I don't entirely like the way that they do it, but maybe I should take a closer look just to get ideas. And what about the Panders? Does their neat little anti-Clan ritual remove the limits of Generation as well, and there just hasn't been enough time yet for the rest of Cainite society to realize this bombshell?<br /> <br /> Also, the <u>Erciyes Fragments</u> are an incredible source. It's been a while since I read it, but IIRC it's one of the best pieces of lore for getting across what a monumental ASSHOLE Caine is, IMO at least. But the fact that it's explicitly written from an IC perspective makes it less binding or credible as a source, not more. I'm pretty sure that the introduction or side-notes make it clear that there are some issues with the history of the Fragments that make them a bit suspect as evidence. But again, that is the post-modern chaos of WoD lore; whether or not the Erciyes Fragments are a genuine example of Caine speaking for himself, or just another case of old vampires manipulating history for their own benefit, is entirely up to the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Also, whether or not Caine makes an appearance during Gehenna is a bit back and forth. It's definitely a prominent part of the Noddist eschatology, but 2 out of 3 of the scenarios in the sourcebook barely reference Caine beyond a nod. You can run a Vampire game without having decides on the answers to all the mysteries of Noddism, but you probably need to have the answers ready by the time you're playing out Gehenna, because at that point you really have to decide whether or not the legends are true.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T13:19:50-08:00","id":1527872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527707-antediluvian-hide-and-seek?p=1527860#post1527860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Eh, attributing &quot;wisdom&quot; to Caine is a bit of an iffy proposition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why that? I don't know much about him but i once found some record of the book of nods telling he was a respected ruler, that he refused to create childe for a very long time because he knew about the jyhad and what it would imply, even tell that they must avoid Garou because they were 2 different peoples and a war agaisnt them would be very dangerous.<br /> <br /> Seems like wisdom but i don't know everything about his story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T16:34:27-08:00","id":1527885,"title":"","content":"Caine isn't known for his wisdom in this series. If he did he wouldn't have embraced the 2nd generation at all and condemed them to his punishment and cause a ongoing pattern of sorrow where is crimes are repeated down through the various lineages.<br /> <br /> The cliff notes are is after Caine murdered Abel and was visisted by three angels offering him a way out and each time he spurned them and had greater punishments placed on him.<br /> <br /> During his travels he encounters Lilith who like him was punished and she showed him how to take advantage of the punishments and gain power from it and when he learned all he could from her and departed. Though in the Encriyes Fragment he used Auspex on her and what he saw truly scared him and he couldn't leave fast enough.<br /> <br /> Later he became a king and did his best, but I wonder if his subjects feared him mostly rather then respected him is a matter of debate for my game and decided to ease his soltitude decided to embrace 3 humans that worked like a charm as they later chose to embrace the 13 members of the 3rd generation and even with his edicts of no more he learned that he had done a bad thing and they inherited his jealous nature and saw what was going to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 01-04-2024, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T16:35:11-08:00","id":1527886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527707-antediluvian-hide-and-seek?p=1527872#post1527872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why that? I don't know much about him but i once found some record of the book of nods telling he was a respected ruler, that he refused to create childe for a very long time because he knew about the jyhad and what it would imply, even tell that they must avoid Garou because they were 2 different peoples and a war agaisnt them would be very dangerous.<br /> <br /> Seems like wisdom but i don't know everything about his story</div> </div> </div> </div>Caine had some value as a ruler, but pretty much his defining trait as a character is being in a proverbial staring contest with God, with murdering his brother out of jealousy as the preamble. <br /> <br /> It's also worth pointing out that pretty much no details about Caine are rock-solid &quot;canon,&quot; and even if the myth about him refusing to sire childer for a while was true, the fact that he went and did it anyways even when he knew it was a bad idea isn't really wise, either. Understandable, perhaps, but not wise.<br /> <br /> Also, Caine being respected as ruler had as much to do with fear of his power as acknowledgement of his actual merits as a leader.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T02:17:54-08:00","id":1527916,"title":"","content":"His story is more tragic than a deliberate crime series , his mistake are understandable, living eternaly alone is an ordeal. His use of blood bond to get the love of Zillah is selfish and totally one of his dark side of course but he also seemed to search beauty<br /> <br /> He tried to give the lover eternity of love, a gift of good intention but he was also heartbroken when he realise that he condemned them to never have what the child them dreamed of, this story was also described as the reaso he was reluctand to embrace new vampires. He did it anyway, yes, knowing the risk of the juhad, absolutly and it will cost a lot for the world but he's no god after all, he's still bonded to humanity by his emotions and failed when he listen to them.<br /> <br /> (My source is the Caine page of white wolf wiki)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T05:53:02-08:00","id":1527920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527707-antediluvian-hide-and-seek?p=1527886#post1527886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">even if the myth about him refusing to sire childer for a while was true, the fact that he went and did it anyways even when he knew it was a bad idea isn't really wise, either. Understandable, perhaps, but not wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the very interesting part by the way<br /> Caine lives cursed alone for an &quot;eon&quot; before embracing his first childe in theory - Eon could be a very long time. Mitochondrial DNA and fossil evidence indicates that modern humans originated in North Africa about 300,000 years ago. Since Caine is the first child of the first human pair, and if &quot;eon&quot; is to be interpreted as a really long time, then Caine could very well be close to 300,000 years old.<br /> <br /> Caine complained a bit about his exile, telling God/Metatron/Michael he will be killed and so on.... so recived the Mark of Caine<br /> The mark of Cain is God's promise to offer Cain divine protection from premature death with the stated purpose of preventing anyone from killing him. With an extra bonus of the seven fold curse <br /> <br /> Caine never really died<br /> <br /> Michael cursed him: &quot;Then, for as long as you walk this earth, you and your children will fear my living flame, and it will bite deep and savor your flesh.&quot;<br /> Raphael cursed him: &quot;Then, for as long as you walk this earth,you and your children will fear the dawn, and the sun's rays will seek to burn you like fire where ever you hide always. Hide now for the Sun rises to take its wrath on you.&quot;<br /> Uriel cursed him: \u201eThen, for as long as you walk this earth, you and your children will cling to Darkness! You will drink only blood. You will eat only ashes. You will be always as you were at death, never dying, living on. You will walk forever in Darkness, all you touch will crumble into nothing, until the last days.\u2019\u2019<br /> <br /> Not even died, but cursed to live on: &quot;You will be always as you were at death, never dying, living on.&quot;<br /> <br /> And more importantly, not even not died, when he recieved the curses... was an immortal basically, livin in the darkness, eating ash and blood. But technically, in theory totally capable to reproduce normally<br /> Not only that, but Lilith tired to help him to Awake, but not really worked, tho the Book of Nod tells us, after the experience with the Archangels, Caine becomes officially &quot;Awakened&quot;, possessing the following Disciplines: Celerity, Potence, Fortitude, Obfuscate, Dominate, Presence, Protean, Animalism, and Auspex. Caine then became aware of the Path of Blood, the Final Path from which all paths stem. And with all these powers, he breaks his bond with Lilith and leaves her.<br /> Or at least the (unreliable) narrator of the Book of Nod interpret Caine's powers as disciplines - but not stated those were really disciplines or not<br /> Just Caine had powers<br /> &quot; I discovered how to move like lightning&quot;<br /> &quot;How to borrow the strength of the earth&quot;<br /> &quot;how to be as stone&quot;<br /> &quot;Lilith then showed me how she hides herself from hunters &quot;<br /> &quot;how she commands obedience&quot;<br /> &quot;and how she demands respect&quot;<br /> &quot; I found the way to alter forms&quot;<br /> &quot;the way to have dominion over animals&quot;<br /> &quot;the way to make eyes see sight&quot;<br /> (And more and more likely his powers were more on the Mage side, altering reality, hence the Curses he gleefully handed out...)<br /> <br /> Here comes the interesting part<br /> The Embrace<br /> Now immagine you are a Fledgeling Caitiff, no idea what the hell you are, what are you capable of and so on<br /> No established madia, works of fictions and so on around, so no Dracule, no vampire mtyhs, nothing<br /> How would you figure out how to Embrace?<br /> Realistically, no way you will ever kill someone, drain her dry and feed it with your blood...<br /> <br /> I think, at this is only my two cent in the matter only, when Caine after an eon handed out the first Embrace to spread his Curse... it was indeed a curse<br /> Or an attempt to give eternal life<br /> A blood ritual, fuelled by his powers<br /> <br /> Why do I belive this?<br /> Book of Nog gives us the answer:<br /> <br /> &quot;But Caine grew lonely in his power.<br /> Deep within him the seed of loneliness blossomed, and grew a dark flower<br /> He saw within his blood the potence of fertility<br /> By calling up demons and listening to whispered wisdom he learned the way to make a child of his own.&quot;<br /> <br /> Caine was the first Infernalist - well not counting Lilith herself of course who had her fair share of deal of Demons and called Mother of Monsters and Demons for a reason.... (and had an affair with Lucifer and had a bunch of Nephilim kids)<br /> <br /> So, the Embrace itself basically a blood ritual devised by Demons or at least they gave the idea for Caine how to do it - kil l someone, rob him of the deserved afterlife and peace, and with his mighty blood, command and trap the soul in the dead body...<br /> <br /> In any case, tragic and fool are two expressions going hand in hand when we are talking about Caine<br /> An old pridefull fool, who is literally cursed to fail in everything he tries<br /> And even then, he could have stopped<br /> Uriel warned him:<br /> <br /> &quot;Caine, though powerful you are, and marked of God, know you this: that any Childe you make will bear your curse, that any of your Progeny will forever walk in the Land of Nod, and fear flame and sun, drinking blood only and eating ashes only. And since they will carry their father's jealous seed, they will forever plot and fight amongst themselves. Doom not those of Adam's grandchildren who seek to walk in righteousness. Caine! Stay your dread Embrace!&quot;<br /> <br /> But he decided to went along anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T11:39:07-08:00","id":1527937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527707-antediluvian-hide-and-seek?p=1527916#post1527916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His story is more tragic than a deliberate crime series , his mistake are understandable, living eternaly alone is an ordeal. His use of blood bond to get the love of Zillah is selfish and totally one of his dark side of course but he also seemed to search beauty<br /> <br /> He tried to give the lover eternity of love, a gift of good intention but he was also heartbroken when he realise that he condemned them to never have what the child them dreamed of, this story was also described as the reaso he was reluctand to embrace new vampires. He did it anyway, yes, knowing the risk of the juhad, absolutly and it will cost a lot for the world but he's no god after all, he's still bonded to humanity by his emotions and failed when he listen to them.<br /> <br /> (My source is the Caine page of white wolf wiki)</div> </div> </div> </div>Caine's story is very tragic, pretty much in the most classic sense of the word: the source of his tragedy is his own flaws.<br /> <br /> I want to make something very clear: Caine Raped Zillah. Forcing her to &quot;love&quot; him through use of the Blood Bond was a violation of her identity and her body. (A part of me feels like I read somewhere that Zillah's Embrace was also against her will, but I'm not sure about that.)<br /> <br /> I don't think that anyone is trying to make the argument that Caine is an idiot or incompetent. Rather, we're pushing back on the idea that any of his decisions are the result of &quot;wisdom.&quot; And maybe part of the problem is that &quot;wisdom&quot; is a bit of a fuzzy term.<br /> <br /> Using the example of Caine's rulings on the Embrace, Caine could have prevented the existence of the Third Generation simply by using Dominate to forbid the Second Generation from Embracing anyone. If he knew it was trouble, why did he wait for the problem to start getting out of hand before making a (seemingly purely verbal) ruling on the matter? For that matter, looking at the power that Caine seems to have over his descendants, using the Clan Curses as an example if you accept those as Caine's work, then it seems entirely possible that Caine could have made the vitae of his childer unable to pass along the Embrace, given how it's a flaw in the Blood that pops up all on its own from time to time.<br /> <br /> The Curse of Generation probably serves as a good example as well. It's hard to argue in hypotheticals, but it seems pretty reasonable to posit that having each vampire's power be capped unless they're willing to commit diablerie against one of their elders seems like something that would incentivize violence and conflict between Cainites. A world where not every vampire can achieve Level 10 Disciplines is probably better for humanity, but that's never seemed to have been Caine's motivation behind cursing the Antediluvians. It's all just spite.<br /> <br /> It only makes sense to consider Caine &quot;wise&quot; if you think that the entire terrible mess which is the history and mythology of VtM is all going according to plan from his perspective. If there was anyone with enough power and awareness to solve some of the problems created by the Jyhad, it would be Caine. And maybe he does in your version; maybe the sorry state of the World of Darkness is in spite of Caine's best efforts to try and fix it, if you want to give it an interesting spin. But the version of Caine we get in the books is more like an absent and abusive father.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T11:48:00-08:00","id":1527941,"title":"","content":"Caine is a tragic, prideful and foolish figure of his own making where it seems that he won't step up and stop his lineage from doing horrible things and in the Gehenna sourcebook we see this in action. The last straw was when he didn't stop Ravnos from going on a rampage and he did nothing and it was humans and other supernatural forces that stepped up and did something and the Big G more or less decided that Caine had used up his chances and it was time to stop this mess for good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T13:37:57-08:00","id":1527947,"title":"","content":"Put in that way, yes Cain is more foolish than wise, plus the lack of knowledge about how deep he can control his blood lieage to curse it make it difficult to know if he could have stop everything by making his childe infertile. In addition we don't know much about what kind of control the 2nd and 3rd gen was able to perform on the blood, maybe could have resisted and knowing this Cain has just punish them as he could, maybe he was foolish enough to just let them be thinking that god will punish them for their crimes (maybe the reason why he did nothing about Ravnos, he knew he would be stopped.<br /> <br /> Hard to say with just interpretation and the book of nod, but we can be sure that if Cain is that old, 300 000 years if our supposition is correct, then his way of thinking must be extremely different than anything we can imagin, maybe he isn't even rationnal at this state","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T13:19:06-08:00","id":1528051,"title":"","content":"The general consensus is that Caine is an absentee father that is ruled by pride to the point that he doesn't want to lift a finger to stop his line from there crimes as he sees himself as the victim in all this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T02:36:06-08:00","id":1528205,"title":"","content":"What I consider is: the Antes are so powerful and so few they got lonely and bored, so they just don't feel the need to interfere. They have no drive after the first millenia or so. And Caine spat in the face of God twice, anything he could possibly do wouldn't come closer to that. They're lonely, bored and sleeping to pass time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T16:25:57-08:00","id":1528230,"title":"","content":"Interestingly enough in Dark Ages Malkavian. We have Malkav seeking out Caine for these very reasons on why the Dark Father did what he did and Caine got angry by it. Not at Malkav's questions but that he couldn't remember why he did this is the first place anymore and said to his grandchilde that he didn't know anymore and neither would Malkav get the the answer he was looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}